 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Знакомься, это Макс  (Meet Max)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "max": "Макс",
  "vadim": "Вадим",
  "vika": "Вика"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Max catches Vika outside the dining room and awkwardly tries to agree that they will keep their night together a secret. Vika is not impressed by how he says it, and then her ex-husband Vadim turns up asking questions, so she decides to use Max. Here is the Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вика, нам нужно спокойно поговорить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Моя личная жизнь тебя не касается.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Давай не будем никому ничего рассказывать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты боишься, что я расскажу коллегам?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я? Нет, мне вообще всё равно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Между нами всё равно ничего серьёзного нет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ах вот как ты заговорил!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Вика, постой! Кто этот молодой человек?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Вадим, ты хотел знать правду?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Да, я хочу знать всё.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Вот, познакомься с моим парнем.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Это мой Макс, мы теперь вместе!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Очень приятно познакомиться, уважаемый Вадим.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's follow them step by step.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Вика, нам нужно спокойно поговорить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Vika, we need to talk calmly.' In Russian, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "нам нужно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"to us necessary\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "спокойно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally means \"calmly\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Моя личная жизнь тебя не касается.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'My personal life is none of your business.' The phrase for \"personal life\" is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Моя личная жизнь",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " And ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "тебя не касается.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"does not touch you\", a handy way to say \"none of your business\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Давай не будем никому ничего рассказывать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let us not tell anyone anything.' The phrase for \"let's not\" is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Давай не будем",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " Then come ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "никому",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " to nobody, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "ничего",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " nothing, stacking the no-words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ты боишься, что я расскажу коллегам?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Are you afraid that I will tell colleagues?' The word for \"afraid\" is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "боишься,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " which ends with a sound showing something happening to yourself. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "коллегам?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"to colleagues\", with a sound at the end for the \"to\" direction.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я? Нет, мне вообще всё равно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Me? No, I do not care at all.' The classic shrug here is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "мне вообще всё равно.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " which literally translates to \"to me all is equal\". He slips ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "вообще",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " into the middle to push it to \"I couldn't care less\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Между нами всё равно ничего серьёзного нет.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'There is nothing serious between us anyway.' Here the phrase for \"anyway\" is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "всё равно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Между нами",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"between us\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "ничего серьёзного нет.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally means \"nothing serious there isn't\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ах вот как ты заговорил!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, so that is how you speak now!' The word for \"started speaking\" is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "заговорил!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " built from an action word for speaking plus a start sound. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Ах вот как",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"ah, so that's how\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Вика, постой! Кто этот молодой человек?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Vika, wait! Who is this young man?' The word for \"wait\" is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "постой!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " which literally means \"stand a moment\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "молодой человек?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"young man\", the standard way to refer to a young stranger.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Вадим, ты хотел знать правду?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Vadim, did you want to know the truth?' Vika says ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "ты",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " to her ex-husband to show they are close. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "хотел",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"wanted\", with an ending showing it is about a man, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "правду?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the word for \"truth\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "Да, я хочу знать всё.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, I want to know everything.' Short and handy: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "хочу",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " plus ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "знать",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " the word for \"to know\", then ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vadim",
   "t": "всё.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " everything. Careful with the final sound, as changing it gives the word for \"everyone\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Вот, познакомься с моим парнем.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Here, meet my boyfriend.' The action word for \"meet\" is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "познакомься",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " with an ending showing it happens to yourself. Then comes ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "с моим парнем.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translating to \"with my boyfriend\", where the ends of the words change to match the \"with\" direction.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Это мой Макс, мы теперь вместе!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is my Max, we are together now!' Two little parts with no action word at all: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "Это мой Макс,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " this my Max, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "vika",
   "t": "мы теперь вместе!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " we now together. Do not mix up the word for \"we\" with the word for \"my\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Очень приятно познакомиться, уважаемый Вадим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Very nice to meet you, esteemed Vadim.' Check out how ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Очень приятно познакомиться,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally means \"very pleasant to get acquainted\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "уважаемый",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
